        {
          "title": "Large Language Models for Agentic NetOps and AIOps: Architectures, Evaluation, and Safety",
          "title_zh": "面向智能体 NetOps 与 AIOps 的大语言模型：架构、评估与安全",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2605.12729v4",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "research_papers",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2605.12729",
          "summary": "This survey reviews agentic LLM systems for network and IT operations and introduces an operational assurance contract that ties each autonomy level to permitted tools, required evidence, independent gates, execution budgets and audit requirements. It identifies a capability-assurance gap as systems move from read-oriented assistance toward configuration change and closed-loop operation.",
